# Shared checkout · clean worktree

**Invariant:** `shared_attended_checkout ⇒ branch ∈ {master, current_unchanged}` ·
`needs(feature_branch ∨ review_branch ∨ land_isolate) ⇒ git worktree add (clean)` ·
`¬git checkout(other_branch) on the shared tree` ·
`sole_maintainer_local ⇒ ¬push ∧ ¬pr` unless the operator names push / PR / publish ·
`forward_only ⇒ ¬move(shared_branch, backward)`.

Switching the shared tip for side work steals it from peer WIP. Lane B already
worktrees; attended seats owe the same. "Submit for review" ⇒ local branch +
`git diff --stat <base>..HEAD` — not `git push` / `gh pr create`.

## Forbidden / Required

| Forbidden | Required |
|---|---|
| `git checkout` / `switch` onto a side branch on the shared tree | `git worktree add [-b <branch>] <path> <start>`; work there |
| Stash to free the shared tip | Leave peer dirt; worktree isolates |
| `git push` / `gh pr create` / ask to open a PR | Local `@sha` + diffstat; land when told |
| `git reset` (any mode) on master or a shared/lane branch; `checkout -B` / `branch -f` / `switch -C` onto an existing branch; `push --force` / `--force-with-lease`; rebase of pushed or landed commits; `checkout origin/master -B master` | `git checkout -b <new> master` (or `worktree add -b <new> <path> master`) from the local tip; local ≠ origin ⇒ stop, report DRIFT; recover by merge or cherry-pick |

## Detents

- Tip already not `master`: ¬ force-switch mid-turn unless named; ¬ switch further for new side work — worktree from the start-point.
- Trivial same-tip edit on current shared branch: stay; worktree optional.
- `lane=B`: substrate worktrees suffice; ¬ move the shared IDE checkout.

## Land (attended)

```
shared tip stays master → worktree -b land/<slug> → commit → merge into master → remove worktree
```

No-PR removes the remote step, not the worktree.

## Forward only

`forward_only`: never move a shared branch backward. Forbidden: `git reset` (any mode) on master or any shared/lane branch; `git checkout -B` / `git branch -f` / `git switch -C` onto an existing branch; `git push --force` / `--force-with-lease`; `git rebase` of pushed or landed commits. Fresh worktrees branch from the local tip (`git checkout -b <new> master` or `git worktree add -b <new> <path> master`); never re-point master to origin. Local and origin diverge ⇒ stop and report DRIFT; recover dropped work only by forward merge or cherry-pick. Kaywan 2026-10-08/09: we always go forward.
Specimen: GIW dispatch ebda76fee569-229874b7 (lane-16053, 2026-10-08 22:43 PT) ran `git checkout master || git checkout origin/master -B master` from its worktree and dropped 33 unpushed commits from hub master. Shared SoT: cortex://notes/system/operational/grok-bot-ulg-cursor-parity.md item 7.

## Anti-patterns

| Bad | Good |
|---|---|
| Switch shared tip to `fix/…`, amend, switch back | Worktree from `master`; merge back |
| Push / PR because a brief said "submit for review" | Local branch + diff; wait for land |

